# Server rights: who may read or save schemas, read or change the catalog registry, read the logs,
# install licence keys and run a request as another user. This file is the only place they are
# read from (-Demondrian.security.file in docker-compose.auth.yml); mondrian.properties and
# -Dmondrian.security.* options are ignored.
#
# setup.sh / windows-setup.ps1 create auth/security/security.properties from this example when it
# is missing and never overwrite it; git ignores it, so git pull never touches your rights. The
# server mounts the folder read-only: nothing reachable over the network can write it (MCP
# set_security included). A change applies at the next request, without a restart. Edit it on
# the host; an editor that saves by replacing the file is fine.
#
# Each right lists the users and groups that hold it, as the auth gateway forwards them. A group
# is named by its full path, top-level groups included: /emondrian-admins, /Sales/WebAppUsers; a
# plain name (emondrian-admins) matches no group. /emondrian-admins, /emondrian-editors and
# /emondrian-viewers are the groups setup creates in Keycloak; add your Active Directory groups to
# the lines, e.g. schema.read=...,/BI-Users. A higher right includes the lower: schema.write
# includes schema.read, database.manage includes database.read.
#
#   schema.read / schema.write         read or save schemas (editors, MCP get_schema / save_schema)
#   database.read / database.manage    read or change the catalog registry and data sources
#   logs.read                          server logs (/logs, MCP read_logs)
#   license.manage                     install the licence key
#   impersonate.allow                  run a request as another user (XML/A EffectiveUserName,
#                                      the Power BI gateway); nobody holds it unless listed
#
# A user matching no line holds mondrian.security.defaultRole; it is left unset here, so such a
# user gets none of these rights. A right with no line would be open to everyone, so every right
# is listed; an empty value (logs.read=) gives a right to nobody. Only mondrian.security.* lines
# belong here: any other key, or a misspelled one, makes the server deny every right and log an
# ERROR (logs/mondrian.log).
mondrian.security.schema.write=/emondrian-admins,/emondrian-editors
mondrian.security.schema.read=/emondrian-viewers
mondrian.security.database.manage=/emondrian-admins
mondrian.security.database.read=/emondrian-editors,/emondrian-viewers
mondrian.security.logs.read=/emondrian-admins
mondrian.security.license.manage=/emondrian-admins
#mondrian.security.impersonate.allow=
#mondrian.security.defaultRole=
